3. Attribution and Credit
All contributors must:
- Include a `credit.txt` file in each character folder containing contributor name and, where available, the original artist’s name and source URL.
- Preserve all existing credit information when forking, modifying, or using content.
- Clearly mark AI-generated content and must not falsely attribute such work to any human artist.

Any act of removing credits with the intention to pass off the artwork as your own is a breach of both this license and general ethical standards. If you are unwilling to respect the work of artists by retaining their names, you are advised to create original illustrations through your own effort. Artistic integrity requires creation, not appropriation.

4. NSFW Content Access
By accessing NSFW-designated folders or files, you affirm that:
- You are at least 18 years of age or of legal age to view adult content in your jurisdiction.
- You agree not to redistribute NSFW content publicly or host it in environments accessible to minors or unintended audiences.
- You will not utilize NSFW content for AI model training or public dissemination unless explicitly authorized.

5. AI-Generated Content
Only clearly labeled AI-generated images are exempt from standard artist restrictions. Even in such cases:
- Attribution to the AI process or creator must be retained.
- AI-generated works must not impersonate the style, signature, or identity of real human artists.

6. Takedown Policy
The repository maintains a strict compliance policy regarding artist rights and community standards. Any request for removal based on rightful ownership or copyright claim shall be honored. Submit takedown requests via GitHub Issue or directly to the repository maintainer.

Valid requests should include:
- Direct links to the infringing content
- Proof of ownership or authorship
- Preferred method of resolution (removal, credit correction, etc.)

All valid takedown requests will be reviewed within 72 hours.

